{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"5b7f2794-0837-44eb-ab0e-33dd57d316c8","title":"Solving a linear inequality on a number line"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"5b7f2794-0837-44eb-ab0e-33dd57d316c8","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Let’s solve this inequality, then show every solution on one number line.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Solve a linear inequality"},{"op":"equation","id":"original","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"-2x+3<7"},{"op":"figure","id":"numberline","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-4,4],"y":[-1.2,1.2],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"baseline","from":[-3.6,0],"to":[3.6,0],"arrow":true},{"kind":"group","repeat":7,"translate":[1,0],"marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":[-3,-0.08],"to":[-3,0.08]}]},{"kind":"text","at":[0,-0.4],"text":"0"},{"kind":"text","at":[2,-0.4],"text":"2"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"5b7f2794-0837-44eb-ab0e-33dd57d316c8","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Subtract three from both sides. The boundary will be negative two, where the two sides are equal.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"subtract","anchor":{"el":"original","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"-2x<4"},{"op":"figure","id":"boundary","on":"numberline","marks":[{"kind":"circle","id":"openend","center":[-2,0],"r":0.1},{"kind":"text","at":[-2,-0.4],"text":"−2"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"5b7f2794-0837-44eb-ab0e-33dd57d316c8","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Divide both sides by negative two and reverse the inequality sign. Values greater than negative two lie to its right.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"solution","anchor":{"el":"subtract","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\frac{-2x}{-2}>\\frac{4}{-2}\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x>-2"},{"op":"figure","id":"solutionray","on":"numberline","marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"ray","from":[-1.9,0],"to":[3.6,0],"arrow":true},{"kind":"text","at":[0.7,0.55],"text":"solutions"}]}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Is −2 included in the solution? Why?","expected_gist":"No; the inequality is strict, so the endpoint is open."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"5b7f2794-0837-44eb-ab0e-33dd57d316c8","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Check zero: three is less than seven, so zero belongs. The open circle excludes negative two; the arrow includes every larger value.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"checkmark","on":"numberline","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"testzero","at":[0,0]},{"kind":"text","at":[0,0.3],"text":"check: 0"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"checkwork","anchor":{"el":"solution","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"x=0:\\quad -2(0)+3=3<7"},{"op":"equation","id":"interval","anchor":{"el":"checkwork","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"x\\in(-2,\\infty)"}],"checkpoint":null}}
